surement but can include focused assessments aimed at detecting abnormal findings that may prompt further evaluation. [Data: Entities (82, 3724); Relationships (7641)].\"},{\"summary\":\"System-level evaluation is represented by skeletal system examination during the physical exam\",\"explanation\":\"The **SKELETAL SYSTEM** entity is defined as the body’s framework of bones and related structures and is noted as examined as part of the physical exam. [Data: Entities (5222)].\\n\\nThe relationship record directly links PHYSICAL EXAM to SKELETAL SYSTEM examination, reinforcing the idea that the physical exam can include broader system-level assessments beyond individual organs or localized regions. [Data: Relationships (11548)].\\n\\nIn the context of the community graph, this expands the scope of PHYSICAL EXAM from head-and-neck checks and cardiopulmonary listening to musculoskeletal/system assessment, highlighting the exam’s role as a comprehensive screening and evaluation encounter. [Data: Entities (82, 5222); Relationships (11548)].\"},{\"summary\":\"Skin assessment can be expanded to a complete skin exam as part of the physical exam\",\"explanation\":\"**COMPLETE SKIN EXAM** is defined as a detailed examination of the skin performed during a physical exam. [Data: Entities (5735)].\\n\\nThe relationship data states that a complete skin exam is listed as part of what may be conducted during a physical exam, indicating this component may be performed depending on clinical context. [Data: Relationships (12884)].\\n\\nThis optionality aligns with the PHYSICAL EXAM description emphasizing that components can vary by clinical context (e.g., what is “commonly” included vs. what “may” be included). The community therefore reflects both core routine components and additional examinations selected as indicated. [Data: Entities (82, 5735); Relationships (12884)].\"}],\"rating\":2.1,\"rating_explanation\":\"Impact severity is low because the community describes standard clini